WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.164
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online TOEFL preparation.

2
00:00:05.464 --> 00:00:08.979
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.279 --> 00:00:17.817
Unit five: Reading: Vocabulary in Context and Inference. Today you will work out word meanings and unstated ideas from context.

4
00:00:18.117 --> 00:00:20.607
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.567 --> 00:00:25.078
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.917 --> 00:00:27.231
Context clue.

7
00:00:28.217 --> 00:00:30.890
Context clue means a hint in nearby words.

8
00:00:31.483 --> 00:00:33.146
Use a context clue.

9
00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:36.832
Your turn. Say: Context clue.

10
00:00:39.667 --> 00:00:41.248
Context clue.

11
00:00:41.983 --> 00:00:42.915
Synonym.

12
00:00:43.917 --> 00:00:46.729
Synonym means a word with a similar meaning.

13
00:00:47.317 --> 00:00:49.363
A synonym of big is large.

14
00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:52.324
Your turn. Say: Synonym.

15
00:00:55.167 --> 00:00:56.295
Synonym.

16
00:00:57.050 --> 00:00:57.993
Antonym.

17
00:00:58.983 --> 00:01:01.633
Antonym means a word with an opposite meaning.

18
00:01:02.217 --> 00:01:04.205
An antonym of hot is cold.

19
00:01:04.817 --> 00:01:07.388
Your turn. Say: Antonym.

20
00:01:10.233 --> 00:01:11.072
Antonym.

21
00:01:11.817 --> 00:01:12.760
Imply.

22
00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:16.841
Imply means to suggest without saying directly.

23
00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:19.554
The writer implies the plan failed.

24
00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:22.570
Your turn. Say: Imply.

25
00:01:25.433 --> 00:01:26.632
Imply.

26
00:01:27.383 --> 00:01:28.384
Conclude.

27
00:01:29.383 --> 00:01:31.766
Conclude means to decide after thinking.

28
00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:34.303
We can conclude that it is safe.

29
00:01:34.917 --> 00:01:37.337
Your turn. Say: Conclude.

30
00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:41.155
Conclude.

31
00:01:41.917 --> 00:01:42.616
Tone.

32
00:01:43.617 --> 00:01:45.523
Tone means the writer's attitude.

33
00:01:46.117 --> 00:01:47.512
The tone is critical.

34
00:01:48.117 --> 00:01:50.316
Your turn. Say: Tone.

35
00:01:53.167 --> 00:01:53.924
Tone.

36
00:01:54.683 --> 00:01:55.603
Reference.

37
00:01:56.617 --> 00:01:59.580
Reference means a word that points back to another word.

38
00:02:00.183 --> 00:02:01.626
What does 'they' refer to?

39
00:02:02.217 --> 00:02:04.823
Your turn. Say: Reference.

40
00:02:07.667 --> 00:02:08.610
Reference.

41
00:02:09.350 --> 00:02:10.351
Evidence.

42
00:02:11.350 --> 00:02:13.930
Evidence means facts that support an answer.

43
00:02:14.517 --> 00:02:16.249
Find evidence in the text.

44
00:02:16.850 --> 00:02:19.665
Your turn. Say: Evidence.

45
00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:23.478
Evidence.

46
00:02:24.267 --> 00:02:28.335
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:29.183 --> 00:02:32.030
Visal, how can I understand a new word in a passage?

48
00:02:33.117 --> 00:02:44.848
Look at the words around it. The sentence may give a definition, an example, a synonym or an opposite, and these context clues help you choose the correct meaning.

49
00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:48.298
What about questions with the word imply?

50
00:02:49.383 --> 00:03:02.810
Imply questions ask about an idea the writer suggests without stating it. You must find evidence and choose the option that the text supports, not one that goes too far.

51
00:03:03.917 --> 00:03:05.626
What are reference questions?

52
00:03:06.717 --> 00:03:17.287
They ask what a pronoun or phrase refers to. Read the sentence before it, because the answer is usually the noun that comes just earlier.

53
00:03:18.433 --> 00:03:20.224
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:21.083 --> 00:03:24.708
Grammar focus: Strategy: clue, evidence, conclusion.

55
00:03:25.008 --> 00:03:26.102
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:26.817 --> 00:03:30.662
The word 'scarce' is followed by 'hard to find', so scarce means rare.

57
00:03:31.550 --> 00:03:34.803
The text implies that the plan failed, because no one used it.

58
00:03:35.767 --> 00:03:43.260
Use context clues to guess meanings, and replace the word with your answer to test it. For inference, choose the option that the evidence supports.

59
00:03:44.017 --> 00:03:47.946
Be careful! Don't say: I guess the meaning without checking.

60
00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:52.271
Say: I test my guess in the sentence.

61
00:03:52.571 --> 00:03:53.630
Test the meaning.

62
00:03:54.433 --> 00:03:57.179
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:57.967 --> 00:03:59.328
A Rare Resource.

64
00:03:59.628 --> 00:04:02.962
The passage says fresh water is scarce in some regions.

65
00:04:03.967 --> 00:04:07.801
The next sentence says it is hard to find and costly to transport.

66
00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:11.694
From this, a reader can work out that scarce means rare.

67
00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:16.279
The writer implies that local communities need new solutions.

68
00:04:17.267 --> 00:04:20.474
The word they in the last sentence refers to the communities.

69
00:04:21.567 --> 00:04:25.580
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:26.417 --> 00:04:28.242
A context clue is blank.

71
00:04:28.542 --> 00:04:32.637
A, a map. B, a number. C, a hint in nearby words.

72
00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:39.268
The answer is C: a hint in nearby words.

73
00:04:40.417 --> 00:04:41.789
Scarce means blank.

74
00:04:42.089 --> 00:04:45.429
A, rare. B, cheap. C, noisy.

75
00:04:48.967 --> 00:04:50.873
The answer is A: rare.

76
00:04:52.017 --> 00:04:53.552
'Imply' means to blank.

77
00:04:53.852 --> 00:04:57.633
A, spell. B, suggest. C, define.

78
00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:03.155
The answer is B: suggest.

79
00:05:04.317 --> 00:05:05.817
What does 'they' refer to?

80
00:05:06.117 --> 00:05:10.699
A, the regions. B, the solutions. C, the communities.

81
00:05:14.233 --> 00:05:16.988
The answer is C: the communities.

82
00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:20.312
After guessing a meaning, you should blank.

83
00:05:20.612 --> 00:05:25.403
A, test it in the sentence. B, stop reading. C, change the topic.

84
00:05:28.967 --> 00:05:32.278
The answer is A: test it in the sentence.

85
00:05:33.467 --> 00:05:36.700
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:39.700
How do you work out the meaning of a new word?

87
00:05:48.517 --> 00:05:50.133
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:50.433 --> 00:06:03.247
I look at the words around it for a definition, an example or a synonym. Then I replace the word with my guess to test whether the sentence still makes sense. If it does, I choose that meaning.

89
00:06:03.547 --> 00:06:05.326
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:06:06.217 --> 00:06:11.922
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: clue, evidence, conclusion.

91
00:06:12.222 --> 00:06:16.361
Today's value is lifelong learning. Keep learning for as long as you live.

92
00:06:16.661 --> 00:06:19.290
See you in Unit six. Goodbye!

93
00:06:19.590 --> 00:06:22.765
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

